<title>GERMANY: Fairchild Dornier to use P&amp;W Canada engines.</title>
<headline>Fairchild Dornier to use P&amp;W Canada engines.</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH, Germany 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The new regional aircraft being built by Fairchild Dornier will use engines supplied by Pratt &amp; Whitney Canada, the managing director of Dornier Luftfahrt GmbH said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Jim Robinson said the Pratt &amp; Whitney engines combined low weight and efficiency.</p>
<p>The new 32 to 34 seat Fairchild Dornier 328 jet is expected to be deliverable at the beginning of 1999.</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom, 49 228 26097150</p>
</text>
